Nautilus project developers are planning to start testing on a new project. 
As per their meeting with the DevOps team, they want to test containerized environment application features. 
As per details shared with DevOps team, we need to accomplish the following task:

a. Pull busybox:musl image on App Server 1 in Stratos DC and re-tag (create new tag) this image as busybox:local

SOLUTION
On App Server 1 in Stratos DC, run:

bash
sudo docker pull busybox:musl
sudo docker tag busybox:musl busybox:local
Verify the new tag exists:

bash
sudo docker images | grep busybox
Expected output should show both tags pointing to the same image ID:

text
busybox   musl    <image-id>   ...
busybox   local   <image-id>   ...
docker tag does not create a new image copy — it simply adds another tag/reference to the existing busybox:musl image.
